  "limitations": [
    "These are shared-host synthetic fixture measurements, not native Antfly server throughput or independent cross-host benchmarks.",
    "The reference server reads and hashes selected values before conditional omission; server storage reads and hashing are not eliminated.",
    "The bounded best-effort descriptor cache can evict or miss under collisions and concurrent writes; those cases correctly materialize full source. Linux wide warm trials include such fallback, so zero-transfer is not guaranteed.",
    "Cold wide-image elapsed time increases on both platforms; identity generation and descriptor registration have a cost.",
    "The Linux wide warm median elapsed time regresses despite lower child CPU and fewer image bytes; no universal latency win is claimed.",
    "Cross-page overlap improves the slow-head cold fixture; tiny-image warm child CPU and some RSS increase.",
    "Warm provider calls are already zero for the baseline. These results establish no additional live model token savings or relevance quality.",
    "Raw logs, trials, fixture libraries and image payloads remain in ignored output; only this compact provenance/median summary is committed."
  ],
